BT 0.1 g /F2 13.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 770 Tm (4. From reading to writing) Tj ET
BT 0.15 g /F1 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 744 Tm (Highlight while you read, then turn the passages that matter into notes of your own.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 g /F1 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 727 Tm (Keep the reference to the source with every note, so you can always return to the page) Tj ET
BT 0.15 g /F1 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 710 Tm (an idea came from and read it again in context.) Tj ET
BT 0.15 g /F1 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 685 Tm (A highlight is not yet a note. It becomes one when you say, in a sentence of your own,) Tj ET
BT 0.15 g /F1 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 668 Tm (why the passage matters and where it leads. That sentence is the start of the next note.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 g /F2 13.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 633 Tm (5. Review and revisit) Tj ET
BT 0.15 g /F1 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 607 Tm (Read old notes when you write new ones. A note you revisit gets better links and clearer) Tj ET
BT 0.15 g /F1 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 590 Tm (wording, and ideas you had forgotten meet the ones you are working on today. The) Tj ET
BT 0.15 g /F1 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 573 Tm (value of the box grows with the connections between its notes, not with their number.) Tj ET
